### Test Forum Real-time Updates

### 1. Create a new post (should trigger postCreated event)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test post for real-time updates",
  "threadId": "1"
}

### 2. Get the created post (replace :id with actual post ID from step 1)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/:id

### 3. Update the post (should trigger postUpdated event)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/:id
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This post has been updated - real-time update test"
}

### 4. Like the post (should trigger likeToggled event)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/:id/like

### 5. Create a comment/reply (should trigger commentCreated event)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test comment/reply",
  "threadId": "1",
  "parentId": ":id"  # Replace :id with post ID from step 1
}

### 6. Get the comment (replace :commentId with actual comment ID from step 5)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/:commentId

### 7. Update the comment (should trigger commentUpdated event)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/comments/:commentId
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This comment has been edited - real-time update test"
}

### 8. Delete the comment (should trigger commentDeleted event)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/comments/:commentId

### 9. Delete the post (should trigger postDeleted event)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/v1/forum-posts/:id

### WebSocket Test Instructions:
# To test real-time updates, you need to:
# 1. Start the server: npm run start:dev
# 2. Open forum-realtime-client-example.html in a browser
# 3. Open browser developer tools to see WebSocket events
# 4. Run these API calls and observe the real-time updates in the browser

### WebSocket Events to Listen For:
# - postCreated: When a new post is created
# - postUpdated: When a post is updated
# - postDeleted: When a post is deleted
# - commentCreated: When a new comment is created
# - commentUpdated: When a comment is updated
# - commentDeleted: When a comment is deleted
# - likeToggled: When a post is liked/unliked
